.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH whether 1  "whether 0.1.0" 
.SH NAME
whether \- Weather for the terminal, the desktop and status bars
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBwhether\fR [\fB\-c\fR|\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-d\fR|\fB\-\-display\fR] [\fB\-l\fR|\fB\-\-location\fR] [\fB\-\-units\fR] [\fB\-\-offline\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR]... [\fB\-\-watch\fR] [\fB\-\-attach\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] [\fIsubcommands\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Weather for the terminal, the desktop and status bars
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-config\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Use only this configuration file
.TP
\fB\-d\fR, \fB\-\-display\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
Display to run (see `whether displays`)
.TP
\fB\-l\fR, \fB\-\-location\fR \fI<NAME|INDEX>\fR
Location to show first, by name or 1\-based index
.TP
\fB\-\-units\fR \fI<UNITS>\fR
Override the unit system
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
metric: °C, km/h, hPa, mm, km
.IP \(bu 2
imperial: °F, mph, inHg, in, mi
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-offline\fR
Never use the network; show cached data
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
More logging (\-v info, \-vv debug, \-vvv trace)
.TP
\fB\-\-watch\fR
line and json: print again on every change
.TP
\fB\-\-attach\fR
Show data from a running `whether daemon` instead of fetching
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
whether\-run(1)
Run the selected display (the default)
.TP
whether\-tui(1)
Run the terminal display
.TP
whether\-gui(1)
Run the desktop display
.TP
whether\-line(1)
Print one line for status bars
.TP
whether\-json(1)
Print JSON for scripts
.TP
whether\-config(1)
Inspect and create the configuration
.TP
whether\-displays(1)
List the compiled\-in displays
.TP
whether\-locate(1)
Search for a place; print a `[[location]]` snippet or add it
.TP
whether\-providers(1)
List providers: authentication, capabilities, limits and attribution
.TP
whether\-fetch(1)
Fetch once and print the snapshot as JSON (debugging)
.TP
whether\-history(1)
Print a place\*(Aqs history: normals, records and the last days as observed
.TP
whether\-climate(1)
How chosen dates were over chosen years, for planning a trip (\-\-location may be any place\*(Aqs name)
.TP
whether\-daemon(1)
Fetch in the background and serve displays on a socket (use them with \-\-attach)
.TP
whether\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
.SH VERSION
v0.1.0
